getArchForCPU: accept a compatible slice when sub-types need not match

ld64 only sets tapi's ExactCpuSubType flag when the linker is enforcing
dylib sub-type matching, which for arm64 it is not: Options.cpp leaves
fEnforceDylibSubtypesMatch at its default of false for CPU_TYPE_ARM and
CPU_TYPE_ARM64.  Fuzzy matching is therefore what is being asked for.

getArchForCPU did not implement it.  On a miss it returned the requested
architecture unchanged -- a slice the file does not contain -- and every
subsequent symbol lookup against that slice came up empty.  The failure
is silent: the .tbd loads, ld reports it under -t, and then every symbol
is undefined.

Current macOS SDKs make this reachable in the most ordinary way there is.
libSystem.tbd declares its targets and reexports as

    [ x86_64-macos, x86_64-maccatalyst, arm64e-macos, arm64e-maccatalyst ]

with no arm64-macos at all, so "ld -arch arm64 -lSystem" resolved nothing
and every C program failed to link.  Apple's own ld and ld-classic link
arm64 against that SDK, so they accept the arm64e slice somewhere; this
is the same behaviour, in the place the flag already promised it.

Scanning for any slice of the same CPU type is exactly what "sub-types
need not match" means, and it cannot fire when ExactCpuSubType is set.

--- a/tools/libtapi/LinkerInterfaceFile.cpp
+++ b/tools/libtapi/LinkerInterfaceFile.cpp
@@ -179,6 +179,22 @@
 
   if (enforceCpuSubType)
     return AK_unknown;
+
+  // Sub-type matching is not being enforced, so any slice of the same CPU
+  // type will do.  Returning the requested architecture unconditionally --
+  // as this did -- hands back a slice the file does not contain, and every
+  // symbol lookup against it then comes up empty.
+  //
+  // This is not hypothetical: current macOS SDKs describe the system
+  // libraries as arm64e only, with no arm64 target in libSystem.tbd, so an
+  // -arch arm64 link resolves nothing at all unless the arm64e slice is
+  // accepted here.
+  for (auto candidate : archs) {
+    if (getCPUTypeFromArchitecture(candidate).first ==
+        static_cast<uint32_t>(cpuType))
+      return candidate;
+  }
+
   return arch;
 }
 
